# No blob files

Do not let a single source file become a catch-all. Prefer small modules with one job.

## When to split

Split (or refuse to keep growing) a file when any of these are true:

- It mixes unrelated concerns (e.g. OAuth + SQL policy + UI copy in one module)
- It is hard to name without “and” / “utils” / “helpers” dumping-ground titles
- A change in one area forces reading most of the file
- Tests would need the whole module to exercise one behavior

Soft cue: past ~200–300 lines of real logic, stop and extract before adding more.

## How to split

- One concern per file: policy, types, factory, HTTP/API client, mapping
- Keep the public entry (`index.ts`) as re-exports only
- Colocate unit tests next to the unit (`sql-policy.ts` + `sql-policy.test.ts`)
- Shared types can live in `types.ts`; do not park behavior there

## Examples

```text
# Bad — one blob
packages/supabase/src/supabase-everything.ts

# Good — same feature, clear seams
oauth.ts
management.ts
hosts.ts
supabase.ts      # open() → postgres driver
connector.ts     # createSupabaseConnector
index.ts         # re-exports
```

When editing an existing large file, extract the piece you are changing rather than adding another section to the blob.
